# Sourced by every luv script: refuse to run outside the Nix dev shell.
#
# The dev shell is the environment, and the only one.  Scripts used to
# re-exec themselves through a wrapper that built an environment per
# command, which meant the environment was defined twice -- once in the
# wrapper and once in the shell -- and the two drifted.  A script that finds
# itself outside the shell now says so and stops, rather than quietly
# arranging a second environment nobody asked for.
#
# Sourced, not run: the exit below ends the script that sourced it.

if [ "${LUV_NIX_SHELL:-}" != 1 ]; then
  cat >&2 <<'USAGE'
luv: not in a luv dev shell, so this script has no SBCL, no native
libraries, and no LUV_* paths to work with.  Enter one:

  direnv allow         once per checkout; every shell here has it after that
  nix develop          an explicit shell, now
  nix develop -c CMD   one command, for CI and other non-interactive callers
USAGE
  exit 1
fi
